# Example local test/dev environment file -- contains NO real secrets.
#
# Copy this to .env.test (gitignored, see .gitignore) if you want a
# dedicated, obviously-safe file to source before running ad hoc local
# scripts, separate from your real .env. Every value below is
# intentionally empty: an empty TURSO_DATABASE_URL makes database.py
# fall back to local SQLite (loom.db), an empty PINECONE_API_KEY makes
# vectorstore.py a no-op, and an empty RESEND_API_KEY makes emailer.py
# a no-op -- see each module's own docstring. This is also exactly
# what devsafety.assert_isolated_environment() checks for.
#
# Usage: `set -a; source .env.test; set +a; python your_script.py`
# or equivalent for your shell, before importing database/vectorstore/
# emailer/main -- the same ordering tests/conftest.py relies on.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
VOYAGE_API_KEY=
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=
PINECONE_API_KEY=
RESEND_API_KEY=
